ns.RawFishing = {

  mechanic = [[
Each zone (and a few subzones) has a hidden base fishing level Z. Vanilla tiers: Z = -70, -20, 55, 130, 205, 330.
- You must have effective skill >= Z to catch anything (so the -70/-20 zones are fishable at skill 1).
- Between Z and Z+95 some casts end "Your fish got away" (no catch, no skill-up).
- At effective skill >= Z+95 nothing gets away. Published thresholds (min / no getaway):
  1/25, 1/75, 55/150, 130/225, 205/300, 330/425.
- Emulator cores (MaNGOS family) implement this as catch chance % = skill - Z + 5, which fits the guides'
  "about half get away at base+45..50" observation.
- Effective skill = base skill + pole + lure + gear + (Forever) fishing buff food, so 330-tier waters
  (Winterspring, EPL, Bay of Storms, Jademir Lake, Strat/Scholo/ZG...) need 300 + about 125 in bonuses to stop
  getaways, and at least 330 effective just to catch anything.
- Getaways go away as skill rises; which fish you get depends on the zone loot table and the water type
  (coastal/salt vs inland/fresh), not on skill. Pools have their own loot tables.
- Skill-ups need about 1 catch per point early and up to about 6-10 catches per point near 300.
- Forever: the tiers are carried over unchanged (wow.gg and wowhandbook Forever tables, wiki zone pages).
  warcraft.wiki.gg/Forever_fishing_techniques says "once you meet [the requirement] all catches succeed", but
  Warcraft Tavern's Forever leveling guide and wow.gg still describe a min-to-cast skill plus a 100%-catch skill,
  so the getaway band is assumed to still exist.
]],

